name: Filtered Review pins and external decision recovery
size: 120x36
cwd: @TARGET
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/large_review.py prepare @TARGET @ART/fixture
launch: --target @TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: findings filter name:0656
require-live-snap: 30 Synthetic Review candidate 0656 | filtered-list
submit: open F-0952
require-live-snap: 20 Synthetic Review candidate 0000 | filtered-pin
expect: F-0952 pinned outside list
ask: Do the filter, pinned identity, displayed evidence and Review action target agree, while full-ledger progress remains distinct?
resize: 160x48
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 F-0952 | pin-160x48
resize: 96x89
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 F-0952 | pin-96x89
resize: 80x24
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 F-0952 | pin-80x24
resize: 60x20
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 F-0952 | pin-60x20
ask: Across the rail, tall and narrow layouts, can the operator distinguish the visible filtered row from the pinned action target?
resize: 40x12
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 F-0952 | pin-40x12
nav-mode:
keys: Escape
expect-echo-within: 300 retained-filtered-draft
live-snap: pinned-draft
expect: retained-filtered-draft
ask: Does the tiny layout retain the intended finding identity and an editable draft without implying that the visible list row is selected?
keys: C-u
resize: 120x36
nav-mode:
keys: q
keys: Down
require-live-snap: 20 F-0001 · confirmed | returned-to-list
ask: Does list navigation release the pin and return the detail and action target to the remaining visible row, keeping the query intact?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/large_review.py mark-open @TARGET @ART/fixture
submit: findings filter completeness:open
require-live-snap: 30 Synthetic Review candidate 0000 | one-open-row
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/large_review.py mark-confirmed @TARGET @ART/fixture
require-live-snap: 30 Selected finding left this query | external-decision-recovery
expect: Showing the first page
require-live-snap: 20 Review ✓ | full-ledger-review-access
ask: Does an external decision recover the now-empty query with an honest notice, without losing recorded decisions or changing the operator's filter?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: findings filter name:0656
require-live-snap: 30 Synthetic Review candidate 0656 | restart-filter
submit: open F-0952
require-live-snap: 20 J104 confirmed | restart-pin
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/large_review.py verify-filtered-review @TARGET @ART/fixture
ask: Does no-color restart show the correct pinned finding and final decision, backed by exactly two explicit writes and unchanged source and observations?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
